Package: nmfLabelTransfer
Title: Spatial Integration of Cross-Platform Spatial Transcriptomics Data Using Two-Stage Label Transferring
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R:
    person("Cindy", "Fang", , "xfang23@jhu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements a two-stage approach for transferring cell-type or
    spatial-domain labels across spatial transcriptomics platforms.
    Non-negative matrix factorization (NMF) is fit on an annotated source
    dataset and the gene loadings are projected onto target datasets; a
    penalized multinomial model then maps the factor scores to labels,
    optionally adjusting for an additional covariate such as diagnosis.
    Cross-platform expression differences can be reduced either by
    projection-time z-scoring of shared genes or by residualizing platform
    effects prior to factorization, and predicted labels can be spatially
    smoothed over nearest neighbours.
